**Done so far (US-048):**
- `engine/world/include/engine/world/partition.hpp` and `src/partition.cpp`: grid cells with stable GUIDs, bounds, asset dependencies, a separate always-loaded layer, half-open boundary ownership, cross-cell and layer references, moves across boundaries, validation, versioned text cell/layer files, and `save_dirty`, which writes only changed cells.
- `tools/asset_converter/.../world_partition.hpp` and `src/world_partition.cpp`: `prepare_world` builds cell files, `.terrain_lod` blobs of distant terrain (one owning cell per tile, LOD clamped), and a hashed manifest. `publish_world` writes them.
- Tests: `tests/src/world_partition_tests.cpp` and `tests/src/converter_world_tests.cpp`, covering boundaries, layer, references, moves, validation, round trip, saving, tile ownership, LOD, manifest hashes, and publishing.

